        <activityName xml:lang="en">Transport, passenger helicopter, twin-engine, Fahrzeug</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Transport, passenger helicopter, twin-engine, Fahrzeug
A twin engine helicopter of the type Airbus Helicopters EC 135 VIP with a weight of 1490kg and a life time of 10000 flight hours is assumed. The average flight duration is assumed to be 5min and an average of 12 LTO per hour are required. Specific cruise emission factors for a Airbus Helicopters EC 135 VIP helicopter is provided of the federal office of civil aviation (FOCCA);
UUID: 9c8b6148-7bc1-3509-9462-6cf5858c3e4d
This dataset describes the demand of helicopter, demand of LTOs, energy requirements and emissions of one hour helicopter flight.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Data is for an average Swiss helicopter for freight transport (6500kg) using kerosene
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: 40500h
Sampling: Statistics 
Extrapolations: helicopter input is extrapolated by a medium haul aircraft.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_9c8b6148-7bc1-3509-9462-6cf5858c3e4d.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
